        <mxCell id="39" value="Refresh paired HC-06 devices" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1e40af;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="918" width="330" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="40" value="⌄ Connection preferences and pairing steps continue below" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#6b7280;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="964" width="390" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="41" value="&lt;b&gt;Connect rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Scan lists bonded devices only. The app does not run nearby discovery. Only names matching HC-06, HC06S or ZS-040 are shown.&lt;br&gt;2. Connecting is a tap. Auto-connect (Remember and auto-connect) runs once when the console loads, and only if the saved device is still paired.&lt;br&gt;3. The HC-06 path is Android-only. On iOS, connect fails with “HC-06 connectivity is supported by the Android app only.”&lt;br&gt;4. “Connect simulated MQ-3 device” shows only in dev builds or when EXPO_PUBLIC_BREATHALYZER_SIMULATION=1. The production EAS profile sets it." style="rounded=1;arcSize=5;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1f2937;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1000" width="390" height="270" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
